{%- comment -%}
Instrument 01: cache address decomposition. The arithmetic in
_js/instruments.js is the real thing, not a mock: it is the part of the cache
simulator that needs no simulation, so it can be exact.

The controls come from _data/cache_instrument.yml. Each is a segmented group
whose buttons carry the value; the one marked is-active is the starting state.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="instrument" data-instrument="cache" aria-label="Instrument 01, address decomposition">
    <div class="instrument__head">
        <span class="label">Instrument 01 &middot; address decomposition</span>
        <span class="label" data-status>Working</span>
    </div>

    <div class="instrument__controls">
        {%- for control in site.data.cache_instrument %}
        <div>
            <span class="label seg__label" id="cache-{{ control.param }}-label">{{ control.label }}</span>
            <div class="seg" role="group" aria-labelledby="cache-{{ control.param }}-label" data-param="{{ control.param }}">
                {%- for option in control.options -%}
                    {%- assign active = false -%}
                    {%- comment -%} Compared as text, so a default of "32" still matches 32. {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- assign option_text = option.value | append: "" -%}
                    {%- assign default_text = control.default | append: "" -%}
                    {%- if option_text == default_text -%}{%- assign active = true -%}{%- endif %}
                <button type="button" data-value="{{ option.value }}"{% if active %} class="is-active"{% endif %} aria-pressed="{{ active }}">{{ option.label }}</button>
                {%- endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
    Three fields of one address, so the sequential blue ramp rather than three
    unrelated hues. The bar carries the proportion and the legend carries the
    names, so a 1-bit index never has to fit its label into 1/32 of the row.
    {%- endcomment %}
    <div class="instrument__section">
        <span class="label">32-bit physical address</span>
        <div class="address-bar" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="fill-tag" data-field="tag"></span>
            <span class="fill-index" data-field="index"></span>
            <span class="fill-offset" data-field="offset"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="address-legend">
            <span class="address-legend__item"><span class="swatch fill-tag"></span><b class="label">Tag</b><span class="label" data-bits="tag">&mdash;</span></span>
            <span class="address-legend__item"><span class="swatch fill-index"></span><b class="label">Index</b><span class="label" data-bits="index">&mdash;</span></span>
            <span class="address-legend__item"><span class="swatch fill-offset"></span><b class="label">Offset</b><span class="label" data-bits="offset">&mdash;</span></span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="instrument__readout" aria-live="polite">
        <div><span class="label">Sets</span><output data-out="sets">&mdash;</output></div>
        <div><span class="label">Lines per core</span><output data-out="lines">&mdash;</output></div>
        <div><span class="label">Tag + state bits</span><output data-out="lineBits">&mdash;</output></div>
        <div><span class="label">Overhead</span><output data-out="overhead">&mdash;</output></div>
        <div><span class="label">Total across cores</span><output data-out="total">&mdash;</output></div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
    Invalid has no hue at all: absence is drawn as concrete, the one palette
    idea the page and the instrument share.
    {%- endcomment %}
    <div class="instrument__section--ruled">
        <span class="label"><span data-out="proto">MOESI</span> line states</span>
        <div class="state-legend" data-state-legend></div>
        <div class="event-legend">
            <span><span class="swatch swatch--filled"></span>Hit &mdash; filled</span>
            <span><span class="swatch swatch--open"></span>Miss &mdash; open</span>
            <span>Events are shapes, not colours, so the five hues stay free for state.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
